WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.740
In logistics, my dashboard refreshed every fifteen minutes.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.080
Back then, it was just the job.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.780
Now it's my research question.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:14.990
Dr Osei Vandermeer convenes the Review Cadence Observatory at Slop University.

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:17.910
We ask how often something should be checked,

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:19.900
and how often it really is.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.220
A beekeeping club's hives, every fortnight.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.080
Forty-two defibrillator cabinets, once a month.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.880
An investment committee, four times a year.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.610
He's the most cited research fellow at Slop University.

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:35.450
One thousand and sixty citations.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:37.040
Three seed fund grants.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.950
And over half a million dollars in research income.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:43.876
Some things need a look every fifteen minutes.

00:00:44.076 --> 00:00:45.446
Some, once a year.

00:00:45.746 --> 00:00:47.366
My job is telling them apart.

00:00:48.566 --> 00:00:49.906
All his work is on our website.

00:00:50.056 --> 00:00:51.056
We're on Bluesky,

00:00:51.206 --> 00:00:52.386
and you can email us.
